 "why_floorplan": "static TP8 collective (OWNER 0ah, no queues/credits): W->E columns = W SerDes faces (ports 1/2) | 4 cross-fold slices R0 | central9macro column (five128-bit S-ring leaves follow cross-fold quarter rows, four P/R banks occupy gaps) | 4 pre-fold slices MY (src E: pairing of dp + P ring; sum W: S ring + sx copies) | E faces (SerDes port0,UCIe). Soft face-register hierarchies are independently preserved; new command pin stage requires one compiler lead cycle. N: in/cmd over the rings, out over the pre-fold column, straps/reset/fault over the S ring. Fold-slice clock entries at each slice's clock-pin row (W cross, E pre); parent glue (~8.2k flops) on its own CTS root clk. Cut: tools/qwen_coll_static_cut.py.",
 "slot_change_request": "compute-die contract v1.2 slot (el1014-qwen-split-compute.log 22:10): S IO band 3,453.4 x 1,563.8 R0 @ x 12,468 y 22 -> this cluster 864 x 950.4 (0.821 mm2) inside it; band order serdes_2 | serdes_1 | collective | serdes | ucie: faces W = SerDes 1/2, E = SerDes 0 + UCIe, N = core (seq_su cmd / in, out).",
 "structural_change": "s1 shared SerDes registers merged across opposite faces (>=744um) and command predecode before pin flops. s2 keeps one independent face-register hierarchy per SerDes, moves all9 macros to central column in864um width, and registers command pins (one extra compiler command lead cycle).",
 "job": {
  "owner": "Codex:q_collective",
  "branch": "codex/qcoll-kv-native-1014",
  "tag": "s2",
  "purpose": "Qwen TP8 compute-die STATIC collective cluster qfd_io_collective_static (OWNER 0ah: compiler command per message, fixed-offset rings, no credits/ready/queues; LU 37 / LS 376 = composed on the real static link RTL + R_max 7). structural s2: three independently kept face-register hierarchies preserve existing cycle, command pin capture adds one compiler lead cycle, width864 central9macrocolumn. 8 CLOSED ot_coll_fold_slice children (coll_fold_slice_rt) on own clock entries, 9 SRAM macros, glue on clk.",
